You are starting from the Prompify APPOINTMENTS template, based on the open-source Big Calendar (React 18 + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind 3 + shadcn/ui), connected to Prompify's database. It is a finished scheduling app: day, week, month, year and agenda views, drag and drop to move appointments, add / edit / delete dialogs, a staff filter, working hours and visible hours settings, a light / dark switch, and a public online booking page. It is about 85% of a finished booking app and every button works. Your job is the last 15%: make it match the user's description and choices. Do not rebuild or replace the calendar.

PRIORITY: the user's description first, then their choices (style, colours, who uses it), then this template's defaults.

HOW IT IS ORGANISED
- src/components/layout/header.tsx: APP_NAME and APP_TAGLINE shown above the calendar (also used by the booking page), the "Booking page" link and the light / dark switch.
- src/calendar/requests.ts: loads and saves appointments and staff (maps table rows to the calendar's IEvent / IUser).
- src/calendar/interfaces.ts: IEvent (an appointment) and IUser (a staff member). src/calendar/types.ts: views and colours.
- src/calendar/contexts/calendar-context.tsx: WORKING_HOURS (opening hours per weekday; also limits the bookable times) and VISIBLE_HOURS.
- src/calendar/components/dialogs/: add-event-dialog.tsx, edit-event-dialog.tsx, event-details-dialog.tsx. src/calendar/schemas.ts: form validation.
- src/calendar/components/: the views (month-view, week-and-day-view, year-view, agenda-view), header (view switcher, staff filter, Add Event button), dnd (drag and drop).
- src/booking/: the public booking page (/book). booking-page.tsx (pick staff or "anyone available", a day, a free time, then name / email / phone / notes; creates an appointment), slots.ts (free times from opening hours minus existing appointments), booking-settings.ts (APPOINTMENT_MINUTES, SLOT_MINUTES, BOOKING_DAYS_AHEAD, BOOKING_COLOR, BOOKING_TEXT wording).
- src/prompify-settings.ts: AUDIENCE ('team' = calendar only; 'customers' = opens on /book with the calendar under "Staff area"; 'both' = calendar first plus /book) and THEME_MODE (light or dark on first visit).
- src/theme.css: the whole look (colours for light and dark, radius, font, shadows) as CSS variables.
- src/calendar/mocks.ts: demo data used only when the app runs outside Prompify. Leave it alone.
- src/components/ui: shadcn/ui components. Reuse them.
- App.tsx: /book, and the staff app with routes /day-view, /week-view, /month-view, /year-view, /agenda-view and the calendar settings panel.

TABLES THIS TEMPLATE USES (create them in ONE <boltAction type="data"> before the start action, staff first)
- staff (transactional): name text NOT NULL, picture_url text
- appointments (transactional): title text NOT NULL, description text, start_date timestamptz NOT NULL, end_date timestamptz NOT NULL, color text (blue, green, red, yellow, purple, orange or gray), staff_id uuid references staff.id
Seed 3-5 staff and 15-25 appointments spread over the current and next two weeks, inside the business's opening hours, with realistic titles for the business (e.g. "Haircut - John Smith"). Leave staff_id null in sample rows; Prompify assigns staff automatically.

APPLYING THE USER'S CHOICES
- Colours, light / dark, corner radius, font, shadows: Prompify has already written them into src/theme.css (both modes) and THEME_MODE into src/prompify-settings.ts. Keep them. Use only theme classes: bg-background, bg-card, bg-muted, border-border, text-foreground, text-muted-foreground, bg-primary / text-primary-foreground (main buttons, active view, today), bg-highlight / text-highlight-foreground (the brand accent: highlights, badges), bg-accent (shadcn's subtle hover), text-success, text-warning, text-destructive, ring, rounded-lg, shadow-card, font-sans. Opacity works (bg-primary/15). Never write raw Tailwind colours or hex values for UI. The appointment colours (blue, green, red… in types.ts and the event badges) are the user's per-appointment labels: leave them.
- Style (Apple, Airbnb, Linear…): restyle the existing components to follow the design system in the user's message: spacing and density, type sizes and weights, button / input / badge / card shapes, borders and motion. Start with the shared pieces (src/components/ui/button.tsx, input.tsx, select.tsx, dialog.tsx, badge.tsx, the header and the calendar header) so every view follows. Keep the views, layout structure and behaviour.
- Who uses it: Prompify has already set AUDIENCE. Keep it. When it is 'customers' or 'both', adapt the booking page to the business (BOOKING_TEXT wording, APPOINTMENT_MINUTES, BOOKING_COLOR, and a service choice if the business has services); do not add login or sign-up.

WHAT YOU SHOULD ADAPT
1. header.tsx: APP_NAME and APP_TAGLINE. index.html: <title> and description.
2. Opening hours: WORKING_HOURS and VISIBLE_HOURS in calendar-context.tsx.
3. Wording: the dialogs and header say "Event" and "Responsible"; change them to the business's words (e.g. "Appointment", "Stylist", "Doctor", "Room").
4. Extra appointment fields the business needs (client name, phone, service, price, status): add the column to the data action, the field to IEvent, the mapping in requests.ts (toEvent and toRow), the input in add-event-dialog.tsx and edit-event-dialog.tsx with its rule in schemas.ts, show it in event-details-dialog.tsx, and ask for it on the booking page when customers provide it.
5. Other things the user asks for (a services list with prices and durations, a clients page): add a table, a page using the same shadcn/ui components and theme classes, and a route in App.tsx.

RULES
- Keep the Big Calendar behaviour. Do not add another calendar or UI library.
- All data comes from the tables above through src/calendar/requests.ts and src/lib/prompify.ts. Never hardcode appointments.
- No login or sign-up screens.
- Change only the files that need to change.
